# User-facing apps the shell's taskbar launches.
# No trailing comments: live-build feeds these lines to apt verbatim.

firefox-esr

# foot: Wayland-native terminal emulator
foot

# nautilus: file manager
nautilus

gnome-text-editor
eog

# Opening the things people actually have. Without these a double-click on a
# video, a PDF or an archive did nothing at all — the file manager had no
# handler to hand them to.
#
# mpv rather than a full media application: it is small, plays everything, and
# its on-screen controls can be recoloured. A GNOME video player brings its own
# chrome and ignores the palette.
mpv
papers
file-roller
gnome-calculator

# Removable storage. Nautilus lists a drive it cannot mount without these:
# udisks2 does the mounting, gvfs is how Nautilus asks it, and the filesystem
# drivers are what a disk formatted on a Mac or a PC actually uses. Without
# them an external SSD appears and refuses to open, or never appears.
udisks2
gvfs
gvfs-backends
gvfs-fuse
exfatprogs
ntfs-3g
dosfstools
# Reading an Apple-formatted (APFS) disk is not possible on Debian at all;
# HFS+ at least is. hfsutils and hfsprogs are gone from trixie — checked
# against the archive rather than assumed, after hfsutils failed the build.
hfsplus

# The installer. Calamares partitions disks, sets up LUKS and writes a
# bootloader — work where a bug destroys somebody's data. It is the standard
# tool for exactly this and is far better tested than anything written here
# would be, so this ships it rather than reinventing it.
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
# Calamares is Qt Widgets with a QML slideshow.
qml6-module-qtquick-controls
